{"version":"6.9","hitCount":3,"request":{"queryString":"\"Clostridium kluyveri\" \"electron transferring flavoprotein\" reconstituted \"butyryl-CoA\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":10,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"24379410","source":"MED","pmid":"24379410","pmcid":"PMC3931072","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3931072"]},"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m113.521013","title":"Studies on the mechanism of electron bifurcation catalyzed by electron transferring flavoprotein (Etf) and butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase (Bcd) of Acidaminococcus fermentans.","authorString":"Chowdhury NP, Mowafy AM, Demmer JK, Upadhyay V, Koelzer S, Jayamani E, Kahnt J, Hornung M, Demmer U, Ermler U, Buckel W.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Chowdhury NP","lastName":"Chowdhury","firstName":"Nilanjan Pal","initials":"NP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"From the Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and SYNMIKRO, Philipps-Universität, 35032 Marburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Mowafy AM","lastName":"Mowafy","firstName":"Amr M","initials":"AM","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7949-2316"}},{"fullName":"Demmer JK","lastName":"Demmer","firstName":"Julius K","initials":"JK"},{"fullName":"Upadhyay V","lastName":"Upadhyay","firstName":"Vikrant","initials":"V"},{"fullName":"Koelzer S","lastName":"Koelzer","firstName":"Sebastian","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Jayamani E","lastName":"Jayamani","firstName":"Elamparithi","initials":"E"},{"fullName":"Kahnt J","lastName":"Kahnt","firstName":"Joerg","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Hornung M","lastName":"Hornung","firstName":"Marco","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Demmer U","lastName":"Demmer","firstName":"Ulrike","initials":"U"},{"fullName":"Ermler U","lastName":"Ermler","firstName":"Ulrich","initials":"U"},{"fullName":"Buckel W","lastName":"Buckel","firstName":"Wolfgang","initials":"W"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7949-2316"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5232-3069"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7645-3706"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"289","journalIssueId":2131758,"dateOfPublication":"2014 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2014,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Biol Chem","title":"The Journal of biological chemistry","essn":"1083-351X","issn":"0021-9258","isoabbreviation":"J Biol Chem","nlmid":"2985121R"},"printPublicationDate":"2014-02-01"},"pubYear":"2014","pageInfo":"5145-5157","abstractText":"Electron bifurcation is a fundamental strategy of energy coupling originally discovered in the Q-cycle of many organisms. Recently a flavin-based electron bifurcation has been detected in anaerobes, first in clostridia and later in acetogens and methanogens. It enables anaerobic bacteria and archaea to reduce the low-potential [4Fe-4S] clusters of ferredoxin, which increases the efficiency of the substrate level and electron transport phosphorylations. Here we characterize the bifurcating electron transferring flavoprotein (EtfAf) and butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase (BcdAf) of Acidaminococcus fermentans, which couple the exergonic reduction of crotonyl-CoA to butyryl-CoA to the endergonic reduction of ferredoxin both with NADH. EtfAf contains one FAD (α-FAD) in subunit α and a second FAD (β-FAD) in subunit β. The distance between the two isoalloxazine rings is 18 Å. The EtfAf-NAD(+) complex structure revealed β-FAD as acceptor of the hydride of NADH. The formed β-FADH(-) is considered as the bifurcating electron donor. As a result of a domain movement, α-FAD is able to approach β-FADH(-) by about 4 Å and to take up one electron yielding a stable anionic semiquinone, α-FAD, which donates this electron further to Dh-FAD of BcdAf after a second domain movement. The remaining non-stabilized neutral semiquinone, β-FADH(•), immediately reduces ferredoxin. Repetition of this process affords a second reduced ferredoxin and Dh-FADH(-) that converts crotonyl-CoA to butyryl-CoA.","affiliation":"From the Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and SYNMIKRO, Philipps-Universität, 35032 Marburg, Germany.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Acidaminococcus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flavin-Adenine Dinucleotide","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Electron-Transferring Flavoproteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Butyryl-CoA Dehydrogenase","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flavins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ferredoxins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Recombinant Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorT